('P', '**How common:** in a U.S. national sample, lifetime prevalence was 0.80% for anorexia nervosa, 0.28% for bulimia nervosa, and 0.85% for binge-eating disorder, all higher in women (Udo & Grilo, 2018). Across 94 studies worldwide, 8.4% of women and 2.2% of men had a lifetime eating disorder (Galmiche et al., 2019).'),
('P', '**Among the deadliest mental disorders:** across 36 studies, death rates were nearly 6 times expected in anorexia nervosa (standardized mortality ratio 5.86) and about twice expected in bulimia nervosa (1.93); one in five deaths in anorexia was a suicide (Arcelus et al., 2011).'),
